cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Taxi-out time prediction for ten European airports (PRC Data Challenge 2026)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jing"
    given-names: "Jiawei"
    affiliation: "Makuhari Development Corporation"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibarapascal/prc-data-challenge-2026-taxi-out"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
keywords:
  - taxi-out time
  - airport operations
  - ADS-B
  - gradient boosting
  - PRC Data Challenge 2026
abstract: >-
  Code and method description of a taxi-out time prediction pipeline for ten
  European airports: a LightGBM/CatBoost baseline of two averaged ensembles,
  an ADS-B ground-trajectory residual layer, a shrunken tabular correction
  term, a label-free drift gate, and documented validation rules. Two
  competition-specific post-processing rules are implemented as disabled
  options and are not part of the submitted predictions.
